From c824e992de9304733aca76d4d996c78aac4b8a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Aw <zachary_aw@outlook.sg>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:18:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] vulkan: add GGML_OP_DSV4_HC_WEIGHTED_SUM kernel

Hyperconnection weighted sum for DeepSeek-V4:

  out[d, t] = sum_h x[d, h, t] * weights[h, t]

One thread per output element over ggml_nelements(dst), walking the flat
index in the same order as ggml_compute_forward_dsv4_hc_weighted_sum
(ggml-cpu/ops.cpp) and kernel_dsv4_hc_weighted_sum (ggml-metal.metal), and
accumulating over h in the same ascending order.

Both sources are read through per-tensor element strides taken from the
tensors themselves, so the model's n_tokens == 1 decode path - where the
weights are a strided view at a non-zero offset into the sinkhorn split -
needs no ggml_cont. A dedicated push-constant struct carries the strides
plus the three misalignment offsets.

Wired through the generic vk_op_f32 path, sharing the elements/dispatch
group of DSV4_HC_EXPAND (512x512xZ split), with supports_op mirroring the
Metal gate, and test-backend-ops coverage: canonical 7168x4 prefill, decode
offset view, padded-stride views, odd n_embd/n_hc, n_hc = 1 and 16, and a
>262144-element z-split. 8/8 pass on RADV GFX1151.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
